From 3a6022c1dd5fce73951f8470842e99d46318b5e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:12:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_expand/lifetime_infer: skip expressions whose lifetimes
 are already inferred

Constant evaluation can lower a `const fn` on demand (hir_ops.cpp), which
runs lifetime inference on its body and then lifts any `const {}` blocks
into new constant items marked Stage::Sbc. Those items exist before the
main "Expand HIR Lifetimes" pass, which only skipped expressions that
already had MIR, so it re-ran inference on the lifted body and hit the
local lifetimes left by the first run:
    ASSERT FAIL lifetime_infer.cpp:951: Found local while adding lifetimes - '#local0

Skip expressions already at or past Stage::Lifetimes (the typecheck pass
skips by stage the same way). The remove_locals validation mode, which
deliberately re-runs, is unaffected.

Hit by deranged 0.5.8 (procs): `pub const MIN: Self = Self::new_static::<MIN>();`
in a const-generic impl whose const fns contain `const { assert!(MIN <= MAX); }`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp b/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp
index 80780e5d..b5088707 100644
--- a/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_expand/lifetime_infer.cpp
@@ -2807,6 +2807,12 @@ namespace {
                 DEBUG("MIR present, skipping");
                 return ;
             }
+            // Already inferred (e.g. a `const {}` block lifted out while lowering a `const fn` on-demand for
+            // constant evaluation) - running again would find the local lifetimes from the first run
+            if( !m_remove_locals && root.m_state && root.m_state->stage >= ::HIR::ExprState::Stage::Lifetimes ) {
+                DEBUG("Lifetimes already inferred, skipping");
+                return ;
+            }
             HIR_Expand_LifetimeInfer_ExprInner(m_resolve, args, ret_ty, root, m_remove_locals, !is_function);
         }
 
